#!   A0_PREVIEW_IMAGE="data:image/png;base64,"
#!   ARCGIS_COMPATIBILITY="ARCGIS_AUTO"
#!   ATTR_TYPE_ENCODING="SDF"
#!   BEGIN_PYTHON=""
#!   BEGIN_PYTHON_DATA_CACHING="No"
#!   BEGIN_TCL=""
#!   CATEGORY="3D"
#!   DATA_CACHING_LIMIT="0"
#!   DESCRIPTION="&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose &amp;amp; Objectives&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This workspace generates an OpenStreetMap dataset based on the user&apos;s location in augmented reality using the FME Realize app. Each feature is transformed into a 3D geometry and styled depending on its feature type, and feature summary annotations are created for each feature.&#10;The workspace searches for local landmarks in the immediate user vicinity and expands the search to a wider area if there are no landmarks around. The search radii for local and more remote landmarks can be adjusted in user parameters. &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Transformers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;AppearanceSetter: Sets appearance style(s) onto the sides of geometry surfaces representing OSM features&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;HTTPCaller: Makes POST requests to the OSM API to query data for the user&apos;s location&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Rotator: Rotates features about a specified point in a counterclockwise direction to face the user in AR&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Source(s) - Reader Feature Type&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;FeatureReader reads in OSM features from XML file retrieved from OSM API query&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Output - Writer Feature Type&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;FeatureWriter writes the XML file returned from the OSM API request as an intermediate step before it is read in as XML&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;FME AR Writer saves the geometry in FMEAR format that is overlaid on a live view in AR&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;To customize this workspace, you can change the following:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Feature appearance (style, colour, texture) with the AppearanceSetter and AppearanceStyler transformers&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Attributes to display in AR as summary annotations with the AttributeCreator transformers&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Location that displayed OSM features are based on by following the instructions in the Preset Location Testing annotations&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;If you&apos;re recreating this workspace with your own data, it is recommended to build the workspace from scratch as your dataset will have different attributes and schema (structure).&lt;/p&gt;"
