#!   MARKDOWN_DESCRIPTION="**Purpose &amp; Objectives**&#10;&#10;&#10;This workspace generates an OpenStreetMap dataset based on the user&apos;s location in augmented reality using the FME Realize app. Each feature is transformed into a 3D geometry and styled depending on its feature type, and feature summary annotations are created for each feature.&#10;The workspace searches for local landmarks in the immediate user vicinity and expands the search to a wider area if there are no landmarks around. The search radii for local and more remote landmarks can be adjusted in user parameters. &#10;&#10;&#10;**Key Transformers**&#10;&#10;&#10;AppearanceSetter: Sets appearance style(s) onto the sides of geometry surfaces representing OSM features&#10;&#10;HTTPCaller: Makes POST requests to the OSM API to query data for the user&apos;s location&#10;&#10;Rotator: Rotates features about a specified point in a counterclockwise direction to face the user in AR&#10;&#10;&#10;**Data Source(s) - Reader Feature Type**&#10;&#10;&#10;FeatureReader reads in OSM features from XML file retrieved from OSM API query&#10;&#10;&#10;**Data Output - Writer Feature Type**&#10;&#10;&#10;FeatureWriter writes the XML file returned from the OSM API request as an intermediate step before it is read in as XML&#10;&#10;FME AR Writer saves the geometry in FMEAR format that is overlaid on a live view in AR&#10;&#10;&#10;**Customization**&#10;&#10;&#10;To customize this workspace, you can change the following:&#10;&#10;- Feature appearance (style, colour, texture) with the AppearanceSetter and AppearanceStyler transformers&#10;- Attributes to display in AR as summary annotations with the AttributeCreator transformers&#10;- Location that displayed OSM features are based on by following the instructions in the Preset Location Testing annotations&#10;&#10;&#10;If you&apos;re recreating this workspace with your own data, it is recommended to build the workspace from scratch as your dataset will have different attributes and schema (structure)."
